   "source": {
    "label": "thm:main",
    "number": "Theorem 6.1",
    "quote": "Let $N,K$ be positive natural numbers such that $N \\geq 2K$. Then, for any $T \\geq K \\ln (N/K) $, and for any BwE algorithm, there exists an adversarial strategy for which $R_T = \\Omega \\mleft(\\sqrt{TK \\log (N/K)} \\mright)$."
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "R_T defined as max over experts of expected loss difference (pseudo-regret); this lower bounds expected regret too. Proof gives explicit R_T > sqrt(T k ln(n/10))/100000 with k=(K-1)/2, n=(N-1)/k. Matches Kale (2014) upper bound."
  },
